extraction_notes: "Page span: the heading (Intel Specter, ISS Intelligence Officer) opens the right column of printed 184 with the lore and the stat block through the O.C.C. skills; the related skills, equipment, money and cybernetics fill printed 185, where the Net Set section begins. GROUP: the book files the three ISS classes in their own Coalition Police & Law Enforcement section (printed 178; the contents list the class as ISS Intel Specter among the CS ISS O.C.C.s). None of the five groups names police. Filed men-of-arms with men_of_arms true to match the other two ISS classes: an armed, armored officer under a military command structure with Martial Arts and three W.P.s, and the book''s experience tables (printed 224) put it on the same ladder as the CS RCSG Scientist and NTSET Protector. MONEY: 3D4x1000 credits to start, printed outright, so that is stored rather than a month''s pay; the monthly salary of 4,200 credits and the free apartment are in restrictions. 3D4x1000 and 4200 confirmed from a render. BONUSES: initiative at levels 1, 4 and 9; +2 vs horror factor at levels 2, 4, 7, 10, 12 and 15. The magic illusion, mind control and possession saves are MISPRINTED - the render confirms the possession clause ends in a stray level 12 with the rest of its level list lost. Read as +1 each at level one and again at level 12, the one level that survived; this is a judgment call and the other two ISS classes grant these saves on a six-level schedule. INVESTIGATION is a special skill printed with its own base (45% +5% per level; the text layer garbles the per-level figure) and is kept as a special ability. Surveillance Systems is the catalog''s Surveillance row and TV & Video is T.V./Video. Forgery''s +10% applies only to recognising a forgery, so the base is stored unbonused. LITERACY is printed bare and stored as Literacy: Native Language (American). Pilot: Robots & Power Armor: Basic is the Robots & Power Armor row with no bonus. Hand to Hand is Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, with no price printed, so the swap is free. The book prints no language line, so none is stored. Streetwise and Find Contraband are both printed +16%, transcribed as printed. EQUIPMENT: as the other two ISS classes, plus plain clothes, stored as the Clothing row. Old style Dead Boy armor is the CA-1 heavy or CA-2 light of printed 104, offered as a choice; the C-5 pump pistol is not an energy sidearm and is not offered. Four E-clips for each weapon are stored as eight. Vehicles are prose; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3."
---

## Lore

Intel Specters belong to the ISS Department of Intelligence and Internal
Security - in effect the Coalition''s FBI. Where military specialists spy
beyond the borders, Intel Specters spy inside the cities: rooting out
dissidents, assassins, smugglers, traitors, spies, black market rings and
terrorists, running surveillance, stings, undercover work and infiltration.

## GM Notes

They are the ISS officers most alert to signs of psionics, magic, alien
technology, contraband and the supernatural, and they work alongside NTSET and
Psi-Net when a case turns that way. Plain clothes and disguise are part of the
standard kit, and many carry a cyber-disguise implant.
